  "meta": {
    "title": "Hawaii's Forbidden Island 🚷🏝️ Niʻihau",
    "description": "Niʻihau 🏝️ is a Hawaiian island that almost nobody is allowed to visit. In 1864 Elizabeth Sinclair bought it from King Kamehameha V for US$10,000 in gold 💰 Her descendants, the Robinson family, still own it. Known as 'the Forbidden Isle', it is off-limits to outsiders 🚷 Only 84 people lived there in the 2020 census, and it's the only island where Hawaiian is spoken as the main language. No running water, no power grid: water comes from rain and electricity from solar ☀️",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "An island you can't visit in Hawaii 🚷🏝️",
      "Would you live without running water? 👇",
      "Which forbidden place next? 🗺️"
    ],
